==English==

===Etymology===
In imitation of a cry. Used since at least the 18th century.<ref>{{R:OCD2|page=1}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɑɹː/|/ɑɹɡ/}} <small>growled /ɹ/</small> (♪: <sub>╰—</sub> )
* {{audio|en-ca-argh.ogg|Audio (CA)}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{context|onomatopoeia|lang=en}} {{non-gloss definition|Expressing [[annoyance]], [[dismay]], [[embarrassment]] or [[frustration]].}}
#: '''''Argh!''' Itʼs already 7:15! Weʼre never gonna make it!''

====Translations====
{{trans-top|expression of annoyance}}
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|ääh}}
* French: {{t+|fr|argh|m}}
* German: {{t|de|ohh}}
* Persian: {{t+|fa|اَه|tr=áhh|sc=fa-Arab}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Russian: {{t|ru|ррр|tr=rrr}}, {{t+|ru|ё}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Usage notes===
''Arrggh!'', ''Aaaarrrggghhh!!!'' or any other variations of the sequence ʻa-r-g-hʼ, all convey the same meaning.

